{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And you shall boil its flesh in a holy place</b> We do not know whether this is a temporary ruling, that the flesh of the ordination offerings should require a priest for its boiling, or whether \"וּבִשַּׁלְתָּ\" is in the imperative, like \"וּמַטְּךָ אֲשֶׁר הִכִּיתָ בּוֹ אֶת הַיְאֹר\" (Exodus 17:5), \"וַיִּבֶן שְׁלֹמֹה אֶת הַבַּיִת\" (I Kings 6:14), according to the words of Rabbi Avraham (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 29:31). And it required \"in a holy place,\" for they are like public peace offerings, which are eaten within the curtains and are eaten for a day and a night until midnight (Zevahim 5:5)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:18:07.435790471Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}